        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 85-year-old female admitted on 16/08/2007 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. Clinical response was satisfactory with improvement in respiratory function and oxygen saturation. She was discharged on 17/08/2007 with oral prednisolone taper and continued inhaler therapy. Please arrange follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. I remain available for any further queries. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
